  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The score of an array BBB of length MMM is defined as follows:\n\n\nLet PPP denote the number of pairs (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) such that 1≤i&lt;j≤M1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq M1≤i&lt;j≤M and Bi=BjB_i = B_jBi​=Bj​.\nThen, score(B)=M−P\\text{score}(B) = M - Pscore(B)=M−P.\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nYour task is to compute the **maximum** score across all contiguous subarrays of AAA, i.e. compute the quantity\n\nmax⁡1≤L≤R≤Nscore([AL,…,AR])\\max_{1 \\leq L \\leq R \\leq N} \\text{score}([A_L, \\ldots, A_R])1≤L≤R≤Nmax​score([AL​,…,AR​])\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, the length of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum score across all contiguous subarrays of AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 5\\cdot 10^51≤N≤5⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\leq A_i \\leq N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN across all tests won't exceed 5⋅1055\\cdot 10^55⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n4\n2 4 1 3\n4\n2 4 1 4\n7\n1 2 3 3 3 5 6\n10\n6 2 10 5 6 6 2 9 7 6",
        "output": "4\n3\n4\n6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : When L=1,R=4L = 1, R = 4L=1,R=4, then we get M=4M = 4M=4 (length), and P=0P = 0P=0 as there are no equal pairs. This gives us a score of 444 and it can be proven that we can't do better.\nTest Case 2 : score([2,4,1])=3−0score([2, 4, 1]) = 3 - 0score([2,4,1])=3−0, and this is a subarray of [2,4,1,4][2, 4, 1, 4][2,4,1,4] by considering L=1,R=3L = 1, R = 3L=1,R=3."
      }
    ]
